Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 21:15:01 2026 +0800

    feat(hybrid): M-ext CSR block -- one CSR drain+verify (ABI v4), minimal

    This is the minimal step of the writable M-mode CSR transport, built up before the completion commit widens it. It advances the include/ submodule pin to ABI v4, which introduces struct hybrid_m_ext_csr and the HYBRID_M_EXT_CSR_LIST X-macro as the single source of truth for the transported scalars. The QEMU plugin drains one scalar, menvcfg (the first entry of that list), and raises HYBRID_FLAG_M_EXT when the gdbstub advertised the CSR, so the flag marks the block as live only on a producer that implements it. The driver's state_diff gains the matching menvcfg verify row gated on FLAG_M_EXT, and its unit test proves the row is compared under the flag and skipped without it. The rest of hybrid_m_ext_csr and the full X-macro drain loop every consumer iterates land in the completion commit.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

